 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Isobutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase which catalyzes one of thesteps of the valine catabolic pathway (PubMed:11013134,PubMed:12359132, PubMed:16857760). To a lesser extent, is alsoable to catalyze the oxidation of (2S)-2-methylbutanoyl-CoA(PubMed:11013134, PubMed:12359132). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11013134,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857760}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2-methylpropanoyl-CoA + H(+) + oxidized [electron-transfer flavoprotein] = (2E)-2-methylpropenoyl-CoA + reduced[electron-transfer flavoprotein]; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:44180,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10685, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10686, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57338, ChEBI:CHEBI:57692, ChEBI:CHEBI:58307,ChEBI:CHEBI:62500; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:11013134,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857760};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:44181;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132,ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857760};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=(2S)-2-methylbutanoyl-CoA + H(+) + oxidized [electron-transfer flavoprotein] = (2E)-2-methylbutenoyl-CoA + reduced[electron-transfer flavoprotein]; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:48256,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10685, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10686, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57337, ChEBI:CHEBI:57692, ChEBI:CHEBI:58307,ChEBI:CHEBI:88166; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:11013134,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:48257;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:12359132};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H(+) + oxidized [electron-transfer flavoprotein] +propanoyl-CoA = acryloyl-CoA + reduced [electron-transferflavoprotein]; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:31287, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10685,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10686, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:57367,ChEBI:CHEBI:57392, ChEBI:CHEBI:57692, ChEBI:CHEBI:58307;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};PhysiologicalDirection=left-to-right; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:31288;Evidence={ECO:0000305|PubMed:12359132};COFACTOR:Name=FAD; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57692;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:14752098};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=2.6 uM for 2-methylpropanoyl-CoA{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};KM=18 uM for (2S)-2-methylbutanoyl-CoA{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};KM=24 uM for n-propionyl-CoA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};Note=kcat is 2.0 sec(-1) for the oxidation of 2-methylpropanoyl-CoA (PubMed:12359132). kcat is 4.1 sec(-1) for the oxidation of(2S)-methylbutanoyl-CoA (PubMed:12359132). kcat is 0.83 sec(-1)for the oxidation of n-propionyl-CoA (PubMed:12359132).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132};PATHWAY: Amino-acid degradation; L-valine degradation.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857760}.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer, formed by a dimer of dimers(PubMed:11013134, PubMed:14752098). May be part of the largemultiprotein complex ARC/DRIP (PubMed:10235267).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10235267, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11013134,ECO:0000269|PubMed:14752098}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11013134,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=Q9UKU7-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9UKU7-2; Sequence=VSP_055780, VSP_055781;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=3;IsoId=Q9UKU7-3; Sequence=VSP_055779, VSP_055782;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Detected at comparable levels in all tissuesexamined (heart, lung, brain, skeletal muscle, pancreas andplacenta). Weakly expressed in liver and kidney.DISEASE: Isobutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency (IBDD)[MIM:611283]: The symptoms of IBDD generally appear until late ininfancy or in childhood and can include poor feeding and growth(failure to thrive), a weakened and enlarged heart (dilatedcardiomyopathy), seizures, and low numbers of red blood cells(anemia). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12359132,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15505379, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16857760}.Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the generepresented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acyl-CoA dehydrogenase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACAD8_HUMAN Reviewed; 415 AA.</bp:comment>
