 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methylmalonyl-CoA mutase, mitochondrial</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_MMUT_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P22033" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MUTA_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methylmalonyl-CoA isomerase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MCM</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MMUT</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5.4.99.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MUT</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_000246</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P22033_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference105834</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MUTA_HUMAN Reviewed; 750 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_B2R6K1_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_02014_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_4594</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Involved in the degradation of several amino acids, odd-chain fatty acids and cholesterol via propionyl-CoA to thetricarboxylic acid cycle. MCM has different functions in otherspecies.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=(R)-methylmalonyl-CoA = succinyl-CoA;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:22888, ChEBI:CHEBI:57292, ChEBI:CHEBI:57326;EC=5.4.99.2; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:25125334,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28101778};COFACTOR:Name=adenosylcob(III)alamin; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18408;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:29056341};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by itaconyl-CoA, a metabolite thatinactivates the coenzyme B12 cofactor (PubMed:29056341).BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=4.7 nM for adenosylcob(III)alamin{ECO:0000269|PubMed:25125334};SUBUNIT: Homodimer (PubMed:20876572). Interacts (the apoenzymeform) with MMAA; the interaction is GTP dependent(PubMed:20876572). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:20876572}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion matrix.DISEASE: Methylmalonic aciduria type mut (MMAM) [MIM:251000]: Anoften fatal disorder of organic acid metabolism. Common clinicalfeatures include lethargy, vomiting, failure to thrive, hypotonia,neurological deficit and early death. Two forms of the disease aredistinguished by the presence (mut-) or absence (mut0) of residualenzyme activity. Mut0 patients have more severe neurologicalmanifestations of the disease than do MUT- patients. MMAM isunresponsive to vitamin B12 therapy. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10923046,ECO:0000269|PubMed:11350191, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1346616,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1351030, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15643616,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15781192, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16281286,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1670635, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17113806,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17957493, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19588269,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1977311, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1980486,ECO:0000269|PubMed:22727635, ECO:0000269|PubMed:25125334,ECO:0000269|PubMed:26615597, ECO:0000269|PubMed:27167370,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28101778, ECO:0000269|PubMed:7909321,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7912889, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9285782,ECO:0000269|PubMed:9452100, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9554742}. Note=Thedisease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented inthis entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the methylmalonyl-CoA mutase family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Wikipedia; Note=Methylmalonyl coenzyme A mutaseentry;URL=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methylmalonyl_Coenzyme_A_mutase&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_4594</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

